'''Mirialans''' were a long-lived, [[near-human]] [[species]] [[Homeworld|native]] to the [[planet]] [[Mirial]]. They had skin tones ranging from [[Color|green]] to yellow or pink to purple. Most had traditional geometric [[tattoo]]s on their faces which symbolized personal achievements. The species had a strong connection with the natural world and typically believed in [[the Force]]. Mirialans included several members of the [[Jedi Order]], including [[Jedi Master]]s [[Luminara Unduli]], [[Cyslin Myr]], [[Katri]], and [[Vernestra Rwoh]], the former [[Padawan]] [[Barriss Offee]], and the [[Seventh Sister]], both of whom were [[Dark side of the Force|fallen]] [[Jedi]] who [[Jedi hunter|hunted]] [[Great Jedi Purge]] survivors as a member of the [[Galactic Empire]]'s [[Inquisitorius]].

==Biology and appearance==
[[File:AdySunZee-YTtransparent.png|thumb|left|215px|[[Ady Sun'Zee]], a Mirialan Jedi with purple skin]]
[[Homeworld|Native]] to<ref name="Ultimate Star Wars" /> the [[desert]]<ref name="Light You Bring">{{EA|url=games/starwars/squadrons/news/the-light-you-bring-short-story|text=The Light You Bring|int=The Light You Bring}}</ref> planet<ref name="Force Collector" /> [[Mirial]]<ref name="Ultimate Star Wars" /> in the [[Outer Rim Territories]],<ref name="TFABG">[[Star Wars: The Force Awakens Beginner Game|''Star Wars: The Force Awakens'' Beginner Game]]</ref> Mirialans were a [[near-human]] [[species]] distinguishable by their [[Color|yellow-green]]<ref name="Alien Archive">''[[Star Wars: Alien Archive]]''</ref> or purple<ref name="Force Collector" /> colored skin and geometric facial [[tattoo]]s. Though typical Mirialans had green skin, some had purple skin.<ref name="Uprising" /> Mirialan [[hair]] colors included black,<ref name="The Wrong Jedi" /> brown,<ref name="To Catch a Jedi" /> and green<ref name="Identity Crisis" /> and their [[eye]]s could be brown,<ref name="Uprising" /> blue,<ref name="Episode II" /> purple,<ref name="Mace Windu 4" /> or green.<ref name="Jedi Survivor" />

Mirialans possessed enhanced reflexes and were also incredibly flexible and agile, traits which aided them in activities such as [[lightsaber combat]].<ref name="Lightsabers">''[[Star Wars Lightsabers: A Guide to Weapons of the Force]]''</ref> As a near-human species, they were capable of [[Reproduction|reproducing]] with [[human]]s and having human-Mirialan [[hybrid]] offspring.<ref name="Force Collector" /> Their natural habitat was [[desert]] or wastelands,<ref name="VE" /> with Mirial itself having<ref name="Light You Bring" /> a [[Temperature|cold]] and dry climate<ref name="Character Encyclopedia">''[[Star Wars Character Encyclopedia: Updated and Expanded]]''</ref> of deserts.<ref name="Light You Bring" /> Mirialans were also long-lived, with a lifespan that could stretch into [[Standard century|centuries]].<ref name="TVG" />

==Society and culture==
{{Quote|She comes from this very... let's say traditional family with some strong opinions about Mirialan customs.''"<br />"''Which involve getting tattoos?''"<br />"''Yeah. It usually happens after you've completed a certain task or... achievement or... something.|Maize Raynshi and [[Karr Nuq Sin]]|<ref name="Force Collector" />}}
<div style="float:right">[[File:LuminaraUnduli-SWM41.png|thumb|right|300px|Mirialans who were part of the Jedi Order often took fellow Mirialans on as their student.]]</div>
The Mirialans were known for their spirituality and strong connection with the world around them.<ref name="Battlefront II">''[[Star Wars Battlefront II]]''</ref> They had a natural belief in<ref name="Alien Archive" /> and practiced a primitive understanding of [[the Force]].<ref name="Battlefront II" /> Because of this, members of the species on Mirial were taught to respect and listen to the Force.<ref name="Squadrons" /> It was a tradition amongst Mirialans who joined the Jedi Order to take fellow Mirialans as their Padawans.<ref name="Ultimate Star Wars" />

Although most members of the species got the traditional facial tattoos, not all did. More traditional Mirialan families felt strongly about the custom. Typically, these tattoos were done after a Mirialan completed a special task or achievement,<ref name="Force Collector" /> and expressed the achievements or expertise unique to each Mirialan.<ref name="Alien Archive" /> Some appreciative of their species' culture considered the tattoos as merely status symbols. Because of her mixed heritage, the half-Mirialan [[Maize Raynshi]] considered either not getting the tattoos or only getting them on one half of her face. Eventually, Raynshi chose a tattoo design with the meaning of "friendship."<ref name="Force Collector" />

==History==
{{Quote|It's a different time, Frisk. We're fighting for a safer galaxy&mdash;sometimes that's what it means. Back on Mirial we'd say: 'it's easy to live your old life over and over, but the new life you start today is better.'|Keo Venzee|<ref name="Light You Bring" />}}
[[File:TheSeventhSister2-SWRebelsRetro.png|thumb|left|250px|The Seventh Sister was a Mirialan former Jedi who joined the Imperial Inquisitorius.]]
Mirialans hailed from<ref name="Ultimate Star Wars" /> the out-of-the-way planet<ref name="Force Collector" /> Mirial<ref name="Ultimate Star Wars" /> in the Outer Rim.<ref name="TFABG" /> After the [[Great Jedi Purge|fall]] of the [[Jedi]]<ref name="Battlefront II" /> and [[Galactic Republic]] at the end of the [[Clone Wars]],<ref name="Force Collector" /> many Mirialans followed an isolated lifestyle in the [[Outer Rim Territories]]. Others, however, decided to fight against the darkness that stood in their way of spiritual enlightenment.<ref name="Battlefront II" /> According to the Human-Mirialan hybrid Maize Raynshi, who was telling a lie at the time, Mirial itself had been the site of fighting during the Clone Wars and was largely abandoned after the conflict, with no one staying behind on the planet to clean up after the mess that had been the war.<ref name="Force Collector" />

==Mirialans in the galaxy==
{{Quote|Green, yellow or purple-skinned Mirialan are another humanoid species you might encounter. Tattoos on their faces are another way to tell them from other species.|[[Eloc Throno]], ''[[Traveler's Guide to Batuu]]''|<ref name="Traveler's Guide">''[[Star Wars: Galaxy's Edge: Traveler's Guide to Batuu]]''</ref>}}
During the [[High Republic Era]], the Mirialan [[Abediah Viess]] was a general at the head of a [[mercenary]] [[army]] of [[Viess's army|warrior-kin]].<ref name="The Blade 2">[[The High Republic — The Blade 2|''The High Republic — The Blade'' 2]]</ref> Later in the era, the Mirialan [[scantech]] [[Merven Getter]] worked in the [[Hetzal system]]. He recognized that attitudes in the galaxy were evolving as [[time]] went on, which he hoped would give him the chance to date the [[Twi'lek]] [[Sella]]. However, he never got the chance, as he was atomized during the [[Great Hyperspace Disaster]].<ref name="Light of the Jedi">''[[The High Republic: Light of the Jedi]]''</ref> Over the [[Jedi Order]]'s history, multiple Mirialan [[Jedi Initiate|youngling]]s,<ref name="Lys'">{{YJA|Lys' Creature Caper}}</ref> [[Padawan]]s, [[Jedi Knight|Knights]],<ref name="Episode II" /><ref name="Out of the Shadows" /> and [[Jedi Master|Masters]] were part of the [[Jedi]] Order.<ref name="Episode II" /><ref name="Dooku: Jedi Lost script">[[Dooku: Jedi Lost (script)|''Dooku: Jedi Lost'' script]]</ref> [[Vernestra Rwoh]] was a Mirialan who arose to the rank of Jedi Knight at a young age.<ref name="Out of the Shadows" />

In the [[Republic Era|time]] of the [[Galactic Republic]] the Mirialan [[Jedi Master]] [[Jor Aerith]] was a member of the [[Jedi High Council]] and [[Jedi training|trained]] [[Padawan]] [[Gretz Droom]], who also became a [[Jedi Council]] member.<ref name="Dooku: Jedi Lost script" /> The Jedi Master [[Luminara Unduli]] and her [[Padawan]] [[Barriss Offee]] were members of the Mirialan species.<ref name="Episode II" /> It was a tradition among the Mirialan people that if any were to join the [[Jedi]] Order, they were compelled to take fellow Mirialans as their own Padawans, as in the case of Unduli and Offee.<ref name="Ultimate Star Wars" />

[[File:Jumping-against-battle-droids.png|thumb|right|250px|A Mirialan fights several battle droids during the Clone Wars.]]
Despite that tradition, there were exceptions: the Jedi Master [[Cyslin Myr]] chose the [[human]] [[Mace Windu]] as her Padawan.<ref name="Ultimate Star Wars NE">''[[Ultimate Star Wars, New Edition]]''</ref> Rwoh was trained by the human [[Stellan Gios]] and would herself take a human, [[Imri Cantaros]], as her Padawan after Cantaros lost his first master, [[Douglas Sunvale]].<ref name="Out of the Shadows" /> Another Mirialan who was once part of the [[Jedi Order]]<ref name="Dark Lord 7">[[Darth Vader (2017) 7|''Darth Vader'' (2017) 7]]</ref> was the [[Seventh Sister]], one of the [[Inquisitorius]].<ref name="Seventh Sister Inquisitor">{{Databank|seventh-sister-inquisitor|Seventh Sister Inquisitor}}</ref> As a Jedi, she had trained with<ref name="Inquisitor: Rise of Red Blade">''[[Inquisitor: Rise of the Red Blade]]''</ref> the [[Twi'lek]] Jedi<ref name="Ultimate Star Wars NE" /> [[Aayla Secura]].<ref name="Inquisitor: Rise of Red Blade" /> As an [[Inquisitor]], she fell under the tutelage of the human [[cyborg]] [[Anakin Skywalker|Darth Vader]] and the [[Pau'an]] individual known as "[[The Grand Inquisitor]]."<ref name="Dark Lord 7" />

[[Reeva Demesne]] was a Mirialan [[scientist]] active in the late Republic Era and early Imperial Era, during which time she worked on [[Project Stardust]].<ref name="Catalyst">''[[Catalyst: A Rogue One Novel]]''</ref> The Mirialan [[Synara San]] once worked for the [[Warbird gang]] on the planet of [[Castilon]],<ref name="The Triple Dark" /> but eventually joined [[Team Colossus|Team ''Colossus'']], and unofficially the Resistance, after opposing a [[Mutiny on the Colossus|mutiny]] staged by the [[pirate]] gang.<ref name="TheMutiny">{{Resistance|The Mutiny}}</ref> The Mirialan [[Keo Venzee]] was a pilot for the New Republic's [[Vanguard Squadron]].<ref name="Squadrons" /> [[Endario Zinn]] was a Mirialan in the employ of the [[Chandrila Star Line]].<ref name="Welcome video">[[Star Wars: Galactic Starcruiser welcome video|''Star Wars'': Galactic Starcruiser welcome video]]</ref>

==Behind the scenes==
Mirialans first appeared in the current ''[[Star Wars]]'' [[canon]] via the [[2002]] movie [[Star Wars: Episode II Attack of the Clones|''Star Wars'': Episode II ''Attack of the Clones'']].<ref name="Episode II" /> In the [[Star Wars Legends|''Star Wars'' Legends]] continuity, the species first appeared in the [[2001]] novel ''[[Cloak of Deception]]'' by [[James Luceno]].<ref name="Cloak">''[[Cloak of Deception]]''</ref> Written with access to the ''Attack of the Clones'' script, ''Cloak of Deception'' was the first appearance of many concepts developed for the film.<ref name="Behind the Cloak">{{SWArchive|url=eu/lit/novel/f20010614/index.html|text=Behind the Cloak: James Luceno}}</ref> Concept art of Luminara Unduli and Barriss Offee was done by [[Dermot Power]], although the two are depicted with chalk white skin Power's art work.<ref name="Art of AotC">''[[The Art of Star Wars Episode II: Attack of the Clones]]''</ref>

The Mirialan Jedi Master [[Jihyo Parrk]] was featured via hologram in the non-canon [[LEGO]] comic "[[One-handed Adventure]]."<ref name="LEGO 53">{{LSWCite|53|One-handed Adventure}}</ref>

